---
title: "2026-06-30"
navigationTitle: "2026-06-30"
---

We've added a new [publish endpoint](/api-emails-publish), which makes it easier to send emails with the API.

Previously, publishing emails required manually updating the `status` and `publish_date` with [`PATCH /v1/emails/{id}`](/api-emails-update).

Now, you can set an email to publish immediately by calling `POST /v1/emails/{id}/publish` with an empty payload, or schedule it to publish by including a `publish_date`.

This endpoint accepts the same payload as [`PATCH /v1/emails/{id}`](/api-emails-update), so you can adjust other fields while publishing.

This change offers a new way to publish emails with the API but doesn't affect the functionality of existing endpoints.

## Example

```bash
# Setting an email to publish immediately
curl -X POST "https://api.buttondown.com/v1/emails/YOUR_EMAIL_ID/publish" \
  -H "Authorization: Token YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{}'

# Setting an email to publish at a specific time
curl -X POST "https://api.buttondown.com/v1/emails/YOUR_EMAIL_ID/publish" \
  -H "Authorization: Token YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"publish_date": "2026-07-01T12:00:00Z"}'
```